e_border\"}"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "The Present Continuous Tense  vs.  The Simple Present Tense"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the Simple Present tense to talk about: </br> <ul><li>things in general</li> <li>things that happen regularly</li> <li>things that do not change</li></ul> You use the Present Continuous tense to talk about: </br> <ul><li>something that is happening now</li> <li>something that is happening around now</li></ul>"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Simple Present \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Present Continuous\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" <span class=\\\"italic\\\">Tonight marks the opening of the Festival!<br> Kindly take your seats.<br> In Salzburg you expect to hear classical music.<br></span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I'm reading a good book.<br> We are looking forward to the event.<br> A soprano is singing tonight.<br></span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "Ladies and Gentlemen"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a formal way to address a group of people "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Ladies and Gentlemen, please look at your programs"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le10ob01aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use when you talk about opera."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "concert hall"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a place for shows with music "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: We go to the opera at the concert hall.